{
  "about": "QAdvanceFeedback per-wheel slip-angle sources. id: one or more SimHub game ids separated by |; * and ? are wildcards (FH? = FH plus one character); regex: starts a regular expression that runs to the end of the id. A game named exactly wins over a pattern; otherwise the first matching row wins. Each row lists four SimHub properties: front left, front right, rear left, rear right. unit: degrees, radians, ratio1 (0-1 slip ratio) or ratio100 (0-100); leave it out to detect the unit while driving. A row computed from velocities (transform atan2PatchVelocity) is always radians and has no unit. surface lists four per-wheel surface properties and surfaceValues says what their values mean (sealed, loose or lowGrip); without surfaceValues, SimHub's own grass/gravel flag is used. verticalAcceleration: true when the game really writes SimHub's vertical acceleration (bumps and hops then pause slip-angle learning); other games leave it at 0, so it is not read. A row with only 'surface' or 'verticalAcceleration' has no slip-angle field and uses the car angle.",
